{"version":"1","source":"Architectural Atlas procedural model","scope":"Angkor Wat, Siem Reap, Cambodia (simple)","title":"Angkor Wat","location":"Siem Reap, Cambodia","blurb":"The largest religious monument in the world in simplified schematic form: Suryavarman II’s 12th-century temple-mountain with three raised galleries and a quincunx of five lotus-bud towers, the central spire rising 65 m.","sourceUrls":[{"label":"Wikipedia: Angkor Wat","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Angkor_Wat"}],"systems":[{"id":"moat-causeway","name":"Moat and causeways","color":"#5f7f8f","description":"The schematic moat ring (real: 190 m wide, 5 km perimeter), the west causeway with naga balustrades and guardian lions."},{"id":"outer-enclosure","name":"Outer enclosure","color":"#c8b295","description":"The outer walls, corner pavilions and entrance gopuras."},{"id":"first-gallery","name":"First gallery","color":"#c8b295","description":"The lowest raised gallery: platform, colonnade walls, corner towers and porches."},{"id":"second-gallery","name":"Second gallery","color":"#c0a983","description":"The middle gallery with its walls, corner towers and libraries."},{"id":"upper-terrace","name":"Upper terrace and pyramid","color":"#bfa67f","description":"The uppermost terrace with the three-tiered pyramid and corner shrines."},{"id":"central-quincunx","name":"Central quincunx","color":"#d3bd97","description":"The five lotus-bud towers: the 65 m central spire and its four satellites."},{"id":"stairs-reliefs","name":"Stairs, reliefs and devatas","color":"#a8906c","description":"Grand stairs, the bas-relief band and celestial dancer figures."}],"explanations":{"moat north":"Schematic north stretch of the moat; the real moat is 190 m wide, 4 m deep and over 5 km around, and stabilizes the foundations.","moat south":"Schematic south stretch of the moat, shown at reduced scale.","moat west":"Schematic west stretch of the moat at the main entrance.","moat east":"Schematic east stretch of the moat.","west causeway":"The stone causeway from the west, the main entrance axis; the temple faces west, unlike most Khmer temples. Exact width is schematic.","naga balustrades":"Schematic serpent balustrades lining the causeway. Exact form is schematic.","guardian lions":"Guardian lions marking the entrance across the causeway. Exact count and pose are schematic.","outer walls":"The schematic outer enclosure walls; the real wall is 3.6 km long.","corner pavilions":"Corner pavilions of the outer enclosure. Exact form is schematic.","west gopura":"The monumental west entrance tower on the main axis. Exact size is schematic.","east gopura":"The smaller east entrance tower. Exact size is schematic.","first gallery platform":"The raised platform of the first of three galleries, each raised above the next. Exact height is schematic.","first gallery walls":"The colonnade walls of the first gallery, lined with relief carvings. Exact segmentation is schematic.","first gallery corner towers":"Lotus-bud corner towers of the first gallery. Exact heights are schematic.","entrance porches":"Entrance porches through the first gallery walls. Exact form is schematic.","second gallery platform":"The raised platform of the second gallery. Exact height is schematic.","second gallery walls":"The colonnade walls of the second gallery. Exact segmentation is schematic.","second gallery corner towers":"Lotus-bud corner towers of the second gallery. Exact heights are schematic.","libraries":"The two free-standing libraries between the galleries. Exact form is schematic.","upper terrace platform":"The uppermost terrace carrying the central pyramid. Exact height is schematic.","pyramid tiers":"The three tiers of the central temple-mountain pyramid. Exact dimensions are schematic.","upper corner shrines":"Small shrines at the corners of the upper terrace. Exact form is schematic.","central tower":"The central lotus-bud spire, rising 65 m (213 ft) above the ground, entered by a steep staircase.","satellite towers":"The four satellite towers of the quincunx, symbolizing with the central spire the five peaks of Mount Meru. Exact heights are schematic.","lotus buds":"The lotus-bud crowns of the satellite towers. Exact profiles are schematic.","grand stairs":"The grand stairs between the levels, including the steep central tower stair. Exact step counts are schematic.","upper terrace stairs":"Stairs from the upper terrace to the pyramid. Exact layout is schematic.","bas-relief band":"The extensive bas-relief panels lining the gallery walls, including the Churning of the Ocean of Milk. Exact subjects are schematic.","devatas":"Devatas, the celestial dancers adorning the walls. Exact count and placement are schematic."},"parts":[{"id":"moat-north","name":"Moat north","conceptId":"moat-north","system":"moat-causeway","chunk":0,"color":"#5f7f8f","positions":0,"normals":288,"indices":432,"vertexCount":24,"indexCount":36,"bounds":[[-1.1747368574142456,-0.012631579302251339,0.75789475440979],[1.1747368574142456,0,0.9852631688117981]]},{"id":"moat-south","name":"Moat south","conceptId":"moat-south","system":"moat-causeway","chunk":0,"color":"#5f7f8f","positions":576,"normals":864,"indices":1008,"vertexCount":24,"indexCount":36,"bounds":[[-1.1747368574142456,-0.012631579302251339,-0.9852631688117981],[1.1747368574142456,0,-0.75789475440979]]},{"id":"moat-west","name":"Moat west","conceptId":"moat-west","system":"moat-causeway","chunk":0,"color":"#5f7f8f","positions":1152,"normals":1440,"indices":1584,"vertexCount":24,"indexCount":36,"bounds":[[-1.1747368574142456,-0.012631579302251339,-0.75789475440979],[-0.9473684430122375,0,0.75789475440979]]},{"id":"moat-east","name":"Moat east","conceptId":"moat-east","system":"moat-causeway","chunk":0,"color":"#5f7f8f","positions":1728,"normals":2016,"indices":2160,"vertexCount":24,"indexCount":36,"bounds":[[0.9473684430122375,-0.012631579302251339,-0.75789475440979],[1.1747368574142456,0,0.75789475440979]]},{"id":"west-causeway","name